**Here is the full park bench speech** from *Good Will Hunting* (1997), delivered by **Robin Williams** as **Sean Maguire** to **Will Hunting** (Matt Damon).\
\
---\
\
**Sean Maguire:**  \
Thought about what you said to me the other day, about my painting. Stayed up half the night thinking about it. Something occurred to me\'85 fell into a deep peaceful sleep, and haven\'92t thought about you since. Do you know what occurred to me?  \
\
**Will:** No.  \
\
**Sean:** You\'92re just a kid. You don\'92t have the faintest idea what you\'92re talkin\'92 about.  \
\
**Will:** Why thank you.  \
\
**Sean:** It\'92s all right. You\'92ve never been out of Boston.  \
\
**Will:** Nope.  \
\
**Sean:** So if I asked you about art, you\'92d probably give me the skinny on every art book ever written. Michelangelo? You know a lot about him. Life\'92s work, political aspirations, him and the pope, sexual orientation, the whole works, right? But I\'92ll bet you can\'92t tell me what it smells like in the Sistine Chapel. You\'92ve never actually stood there and looked up at that beautiful ceiling. Seen that.  \
\
If I ask you about women, you\'92d probably give me a syllabus about your personal favorites. You may have even been laid a few times. But you can\'92t tell me what it feels like to wake up next to a woman and feel truly happy.  \
\
You\'92re a tough kid. And I\'92d ask you about war, you\'92d probably throw Shakespeare at me, right? \'93Once more unto the breach, dear friends.\'94 But you\'92ve never been near one. You\'92ve never held your best friend\'92s head in your lap\'85 watch him gasp his last breath looking to you for help.  \
\
I\'92d ask you about love, you\'92d probably quote me a sonnet. But you\'92ve never looked at a woman and been totally vulnerable. Known someone that could level you with her eyes. Feeling like God put an angel on Earth just for you\'85 who could rescue you from the depths of hell. And you wouldn\'92t know what it\'92s like to be her angel, to have that love for her, be there forever\'85 through anything\'85 through cancer. And you wouldn\'92t know about sleeping sitting up in a hospital room for two months, holding her hand, because the doctors could see in your eyes that the terms \'93visiting hours\'94 don\'92t apply to you.  \
\
You don\'92t know about real loss, \'92cause that only occurs when you love something more than you love yourself. And I doubt you\'92ve ever dared to love anybody that much.  \
\
And look at you. I don\'92t see an intelligent, confident man. I see a cocky, scared shitless kid. But you\'92re a genius, Will. No one denies that. No one could possibly understand the depths of you. But you presume to know everything about me because you saw a painting of mine and you ripped my fucking life apart. You\'92re an orphan, right?\
